  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "The value of an investment is growing at a rate of 6% per year. The initial investment is valued at $\\$500$. To the nearest year, determine how long it will take for the investment to be valued at $\\$4000$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$36$ years.",
      "worked": "Let $V(t)$ be the investment value in dollars after $t$ years. The annual growth factor is $1.06$, so $V(t)=500(1.06)^t$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}500(1.06)^t&=4000\\\\(1.06)^t&=8\\\\\\log_{10}(1.06)^t&=\\log_{10}8\\\\t\\log_{10}1.06&=\\log_{10}8\\\\t&=\\frac{\\log_{10}8}{\\log_{10}1.06}\\\\t&\\approx35.69\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe investment will reach $\\$4000$ after approximately $36$ years, to the nearest year.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 48
  },
